Z||000000||fierobaby||10-19-2001||04:03 PM||||ok my father claims my battery is dead.... but the radio workds perfect... the clock is fine...it chimes (like when you leave your lights on) fine... when my moms dies her car was not doing any of that... so is it the battery?<P>------------------<BR>:wtf: <FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87 :wtf:<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||10-19-2001||04:09 PM||||Depends on just HOW dead the battery is.  I've seen batteries have enough juice for dome lights and radios, but not enough to turn the car over, so it's not outside the realm of possibility.  Then again, every once and again you'll see a battery so dead that nothing works.<P>Swap in a new one and see if it solves the problem.<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-19-2001||04:14 PM||||Exactly what is your car doing that makes him believe the battery is dead?||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||10-19-2001||05:30 PM||||Is this a continuation of the problem you posted a few weeks ago? Bad batteries show up several different ways.<BR>1. Won't take a charge-battery is always near 'dead'. usually internal connection between the cells is gone. Shows 0 or way less than 13.5 volts with a voltmeter across the posts. Usually wont even light the interior lights.<BR>2. Low 'water' level. Battery will smell like rotten eggs while charging. Won't take  a charge either. Even in maint-free batteries, you can usually pry off the top to check it. (can't do this on all of em)<BR>3.Warped or corroded plates. Battery will charge up to full, but will not hold a full charge. Cranks the eng over well at first but soon slows way down if eng doesn't start right off. No reserve cranking amps. Shows up when you leave the headlights on for a very short time with eng off and the battery won't start the car. Battery actually 'died' in the heat of the summer, but as cold weather aproaches, it manifests itself as above. Got one in my Jeep right now just like this. Does fine if I fully charge it, but won't last long if it takes very long to start the engine. What it amounts to is trying to use a 12 vlt lawnmower battery to start your Fiero. It will show 13 volts, but there simply isn't enough plate area to have suffiecent cranking amps in reserve. Sounds like what you have. Have it checked with a load type tester at autozone. Or, you could 'borrow' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> your Mom's battery for a few weeks and see if the problem goes away in your car and starts showing itself in her's. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bazooka||10-20-2001||12:32 PM||||Fierobaby,     The best way to see if your battery is gone is to do a HEAVY LOAD TEST. First charge up your battery. Then without turning the engine on, remove the Surface Charge by turning on all your accesories like the heater fan, all lights, radio, rear window defogger, etc. for 2 1/2 minute period. Now you can check available voltage across the battery terminals and that should not be under 10 volts. If it is under then throw away the battery if over then you can still recharge it. The ECM needs about 10 1/2 volts to hold its memory and healthy batteries should show about 12 volts at this point. When running it can be 13.4 minimum.<BR>***************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>**************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DrDave||10-20-2001||04:53 PM||||Go for the easy stuff first.  If the battery contgacts are dirty, the radio and such can work but not enought amperage will be aviailable to crank the starter.||||reg||1
Z||000006||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-20-2001||05:23 PM||||turn on the headlights... if they are bright..batterys good...dim..batterys dead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||10-20-2001||09:41 PM||||Is your starter OK. Clean battery terminals and charge it. turn on headlites and then use starter and see if the lites go out. Dont buy expensive battery with a zillion year warranty. They all die in 3-5 years. Ive had $160 ones in my Mercedes and they gave up same in length of time as Autozone $39.95. Also check out your alt, should put out around 13.5-14 volts running with AC and lights on. use a meter at terminials, not the car gauge.||||reg||1
Z||000008||SLYGUY||10-21-2001||01:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>turn on the headlights... if they are bright..batterys good...dim..batterys dead   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>NOW THAT IS SOME GENIUS!!!<BR>LOL<P>Good luck with the battery. I'd change it with your mom's car too. See if it is just your battery. <BR>Clean them terminals too!!<P>Sly||||reg||1
