Z||000010||JohnF||10-21-2001||10:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>turn on the headlights... if they are bright..battery's good...dim..battery's dead   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Like was said earlier - do the easy stuff FIRST!<P>Try this test.  It eithjer is the battery or it isn't.  This will tell.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-21-2001||10:48 AM||||<BR>Does it do it when its hot only? if so, its starter getting warm and a heatshield may help, but if its all the time, hot/cold, it sounds like the battery needs a deep cell charge.<P>take it to a local garage and ask them to do a deep cell charge for you (will take overnight) and they may charge a few $ for doing it..<BR>If it is happening overnight, maybe something is draining the battery, quick way to find out.. turn everything off, then unplug a battery cable, hold a voltage tester between the cable and the battery, if it lights..there is a drain.. it it dont..you are good to go..<BR>If it does light, remove one fuse at a time and watch for when the light goes out, when it goes out, you found your problem item that is draining your battery.<P>I had to do that recently and found out my alarm was sucking power. <P>good luck!||||reg||1
